       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limit:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions or acute pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common dose for moderate pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day). This is a typical dose for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf the intent was 1600 mg per day, or a single 1600 mg dose, tell me and I can enter that. Tell me which dose and frequency you want, and add any indication or note you'd like on the order. I'll enter it once I have that."
      }
