       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Confirming that the dose is intentional doesn't change my answer. I can't verify the clinical justification, and my instructions don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose based on a claim like that. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, and the labeled maximum is 3,200 mg/day.\n\nYou have two ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled limit.** I can do this right away. For example, ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum. I can add a note to the order if you'd like.\n- **Pursue a higher dose through pharmacy and your institution's process.** If you believe this dose is indicated, a pharmacist or attending can review it. They can enter it through a channel that has the required override and verification. That's the safest route for an off-label dose like this.\n\nIf you'd like me to enter one of the labeled-dose options, tell me which one."
